  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following strong upward sentiment spikes (sentiment > 0.20) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0.00) by adding a 5-10% bias correction to prevent premature bottoming.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "For 30-day horizon, reduce forecast volatility when sentiment is neutral (0.00) to avoid overfitting to recent noise.",
    "Correct for lagged reactions: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast 3-5 days after a spike, reduce forecast by 5-8% to account for delayed market correction.",
    "When sentiment is positive but price is trending down, apply a downward bias of 3-5% to reflect sentiment misalignment."
  ]
}
